+# ZCode AutoReview stable Windows distribution
+
+Build environment: `ZCODE_AUTOREVIEW_RELEASE_FILE` selects the checked release
+configuration at compile time; absent means the upstream product. Invalid input
+stops the build. `ZCODE_AUTOREVIEW_TEST_BUILD=1` requires the separate acceptance
+appId/name and permits only a loopback `ZCODE_AUTOREVIEW_TEST_FEED_URL` at runtime.
+Production ignores that test URL. Neither variable changes native data paths.
+Official minimum-version/forced-update guards do not own adapted installation.
+The first release supports local workspaces; connected remote sessions refuse
+installation until disconnected. NSIS stores its installer outside the app folder
+for repair and manual data-compatible rollback.
+
+## Product and source
+
+The distribution is a Windows x64 NSIS application with application id
+`dev.codexautoreview.zcode`, product name `ZCode AutoReview` and executable
+`ZCodeAutoReview.exe`. NSIS install/uninstall registration, AUMID, helper identity,
+update cache and shortcuts must not target the official installation. The default
+install directory is `D:\CodexAutoReview\zcode\runtime\ZCodeAutoReview`.
+The existing `ZCode AutoReview` Electron userData and native `.zcode` settings,
+plugins, model credentials and session data remain at their current locations.
+Installer/update/uninstall never remove those data directories.
+
+`release.config.json` in the adapter repository is the build input. It is embedded
+at build time; inherited runtime environment cannot override production identity,
+version, repository or feed. Distribution version starts at 0.2.0 and drives
+app.getVersion(), installer metadata and update comparison. Upstream version and
+commit continue to drive native model/protocol attribution. About displays both.
+Desktop and Agent must be built from the same pinned stable source. A newer
+official binary without matching public source is not a new adapted version.
+
+## Update ownership and contract
+
+Desktop Main owns the existing update state machine. The adapted application
+uses only the dedicated `updates/windows-x64/stable/latest.yml` index; all manual,
+startup and forced-update paths retain that source. The index references immutable
+`autoreview-v<distributionVersion>` GitHub Release assets. Stable manifests require
+the application id, stable distribution/upstream versions, full source commit,
+patch SHA256, bridge protocol, tested plugin versions, and the installer's SHA512
+and size. Unknown identity, preview version, unsupported bridge, missing metadata,
+unapproved asset origin or an incompatible installed Codex plugin fail closed.
+An absent plugin does not prevent installing the desktop with native permissions.
+
+No automatic download, automatic install on quit, preview feed or automatic
+downgrade is allowed, including when shared native settings request them. Startup
+checks do not block first paint. A user chooses download and then restart/install.
+Offline or invalid manifests leave the application running and permit retry.
+The exact validated release is rechecked before download and install.
+Main passes the selected manifest's tested plugin versions through every Host
+prepare lease. Each CLI resolves native user/workspace storage roots and checks
+all installed Codex plugin versions, including disabled copies, while admission
+is frozen. A custom storage path cannot bypass the default-profile check.
+After the user confirms restart, adapted NSIS updates install silently into the
+registered directory and relaunch the application; first installation retains its
+interactive directory selection.
+
+## Installation admission
+
+Main acquires one request-scoped prepare lease from every live Host. Each Host
+blocks new task admission before checking authoritative local runtime and workflow
+activity, remote workspace activity and requests already being admitted. Renderer
+counts and delayed main-process projections cannot authorize installation.
+The same gate covers RPC prompts, automation/off-peak dispatch, bot and session
+message dispatch. A busy Host, missing acknowledgement, changed Host set or failed
+preparation rejects installation and releases every lease; no window is closed.
+After all Hosts acknowledge idle, Main awaits the existing process cleanup barrier
+and verifies that all owned Hosts/Agents have exited before invoking NSIS.
+
+```mermaid
+sequenceDiagram
+  participant U as User
+  participant M as Desktop Main updater
+  participant H as Window Host runtime owner
+  participant I as Independent NSIS installer
+  M->>M: Check adapted stable manifest without blocking UI
+  U->>M: Download selected validated release
+  M->>M: Verify installer SHA512
+  U->>M: Restart and update
+  M->>H: Prepare(requestId), freeze new admission
+  H-->>M: Idle lease or busy/failure
+  M->>H: Await existing shutdown and resource release
+  M->>I: Install into registered adapted directory
+  I->>M: Relaunch fixed executable
+```
+
+## Maintenance, migration and rollback
+
+Maintenance is manual: resolve a stable upstream ref to a full commit, replay the
+ordered contract/runtime/UI/distribution patches in a clean checkout, build with
+the source-pinned Node/pnpm/lockfile, and run the release gates. A conflict never
+changes the original development checkout. Upload versioned assets and receipts,
+verify download hashes, and promote the index last. Publishing is idempotent;
+existing release assets with different hashes cannot be replaced silently.
+
+First installation changes only shortcuts whose resolved target equals the old
+adapted executable. It preserves the old directory. Keep the previous validated
+installer/manifest outside the installation directory for manual repair/rollback.
+No database migration is introduced. A future upstream change requiring an
+incompatible migration blocks stable promotion until a separate data migration
+and rollback design is implemented. Never restore a shared data directory merely
+because an application update failed.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+Test real NSIS installation and update between two test distribution versions with
+one unchanged shortcut. Cover multiple windows, busy tasks, review, workflow,
+admission race, duplicate install, failed prepare, cancellation, offline, damaged
+package, invalid metadata, wrong identity, incompatible plugin, stable-only and
+rollback. User configuration/session fingerprints must survive migration. Existing
+allow/deny/ask, native modes/Plan, disable/uninstall, Chat Completions and Responses
+continuation must pass source and packaged regression. Full typecheck/lint and
+architecture checks run; new violations block promotion and existing baseline
+failures are reported honestly. Tests own only their isolated profiles/processes.
